  "slug": "cryo-em-4dfe",
  "summary": "Atomistic MD, weighted-ensemble sampling, and cryo-EM thermodynamics now resolve conformational transitions as explicit pathways rather than static states.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is treating conformational change as an explicit pathway rather than a static endpoint. Atomistic MD of intact and ND4/ND5-truncated complex I shows a ND2 P-side conformational change that occurs more readily in the truncated model, with local changes reported. For the human voltage-gated proton channel hHV1, the activation pathway is resolved by integrating constant-pH MD, weighted-ensemble sampling, and AlphaFold modeling. A cryo-EM method combining iterative 3D classification, simulated-particle error quantification, and global thermodynamic modeling extracts minute energy differences among heterogeneous complexes. What is new is pairing enhanced sampling and thermodynamic readouts with pathway-level interpretation for membrane proteins. A PDB survey using Cremer-Pople puckering coordinates adds a caution: pyranose ring distortions may reflect experimental conditions rather than biology.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-09"
}
